        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40663</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40663"/>
        <updated>2025-08-08T08:43:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 139 adds support for the <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#corner-shaping" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">corner-shape</code></a> property, and its related shorthands and longhands. See <a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/5357329815699456" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5357329815699456</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This PR adds:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>A <code class="notranslate">corner-shape</code> reference page</li>
<li>Reference pages for all of its many constituent properties and related shorthands.</li>
<li>A <code class="notranslate">&lt;corner-shape-value&gt;</code> data type ref page.</li>
<li>A <code class="notranslate">superellipse()</code> function ref page.</li>
<li>Mentions of the new data type and function in the appropriate places.</li>
</ul>

<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

